   "prompt": "Goal: cut wasted cultivation volume at p = 0.002 without raising infidelity\nA 9-qubit magic-state cultivation stage runs 3 syndrome rounds with 198 checks at physical error rate 0.002. After each of the first 2 rounds you may abort if the cumulative syndrome weight exceeds a threshold (99 means never abort). At the end you accept if the final weight is at or below a final threshold.\nThe fixed baseline F never aborts and accepts only weight 0, scoring W = 78.1909 and infidelity = 0.000552798. Propose abort thresholds (99 means never abort) and a final accept threshold that cut wasted spacetime volume per accepted output without raising output infidelity above the baseline bound, and say why in one sentence.",
